{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger","id":964083,"title":"Changeling 2E Japan (Kinda Like Tokyo, Only Bigger)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-05T22:24:20-07:00","id":964083,"title":"Changeling 2E Japan (Kinda Like Tokyo, Only Bigger)","content":"Hey. I haven't updated in a while. I'm knee-deep in final revisions. But, I thought I'd share something with you. This is Japan for the Lost. Or at least Honshu. You know, in the vein of the Tokyo bits I've been doing for (insert every book title pretty much). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyoRXgtUjI0alAyc0E\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyoRXgtUjI0alAyc0E\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyoRXgtUjI0alAyc0E\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyoRXgtUjI0alAyc0E </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:13:25-07:00","id":964095,"title":"","content":"Is it offensive if I say that this is the best Japan writeup so far? Because I love everything about this. Each of the envoys leaps off the page as a ready chronicle in their own right (playing Ayumi Yamada's misfit band of investigators would be a blast, as would Yuicihi Okamoto's &quot;hostage negotiator&quot; approach to Werewolf diplomacy) and there's so many ready little hooks to run this.<br /> <br /> Considering I came at Changeling 2e as a hater originally, it speaks volumes that it's now one of the books I'm most excited for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:15:42-07:00","id":964096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964095#post964095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it offensive if I say that this is the best Japan writeup so far? Because I love everything about this. Each of the envoys leaps off the page as a ready chronicle in their own right (playing Ayumi Yamada's misfit band of investigators would be a blast, as would Yuicihi Okamoto's &quot;hostage negotiator&quot; approach to Werewolf diplomacy) and there's so many ready little hooks to run this.<br /> <br /> Considering I came at Changeling 2e as a hater originally, it speaks volumes that it's now one of the books I'm most excited for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm super glad to hear all of this. Not at all offensive.<br /> <br /> And yeah. I really wanted to make a ton of inherent story hooks and basically motleys ready to make, so you could just jump right in and have plenty of ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:20:46-07:00","id":964102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964096#post964096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm super glad to hear all of this. Not at all offensive.<br /> <br /> And yeah. I really wanted to make a ton of inherent story hooks and basically motleys ready to make, so you could just jump right in and have plenty of ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>To peak behind the curtain a bit, how did you settle on the three major Courts? I didn't expect a retread of the Directionals (though a 2e update eventually would be heavenly - or was the Three Kingdoms setting 2e-compatible?), but Defiance, Conformity/Tradition, and Harmony are unique picks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:28:01-07:00","id":964107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964102#post964102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To peak behind the curtain a bit, how did you settle on the three major Courts? I didn't expect a retread of the Directionals (though a 2e update eventually would be heavenly - or was the Three Kingdoms setting 2e-compatible?), but Defiance, Conformity/Tradition, and Harmony are unique picks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was literally it. I wanted something unique, that people weren't expecting. So, I toyed around with a few ideas. I definitely didn't want to do Directional Courts, since they're more Chinese in basic feeling. So, I settled with doing something that was a triad that looks maybe &quot;balanced&quot; from the outside, but has inherent, implicit biases and conflicts that'll rise in play.<br /> <br /> And yes, you'll see Directional Courts. I've got to look at Three Kingdoms. I don't know if it is or not. But, I have plans for future books to touch on that stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:31:44-07:00","id":964109,"title":"","content":"Why did you choose Tokyo to be the largest court/ population center for the Changelings/Lost and not a city like Beijing, Nanjing, or Shanghai? Chinese influence can be found in most of East Asia. Also, the Japan is dealing with a worse population decline than any other country in East Asia. It's not that I disapprove of Tokyo being the biggest metropolitan center for Changelings, but I am curious to see if you use some historical event to explain this like China's Great Leap Forward, the Cultural Revolution, or even the Bamboo curtain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:33:16-07:00","id":964110,"title":"","content":"My changeling character is a fire rat when it comes to the Zodiac, and has a rather rebellious attitude, so if he ever travels to Japan I'll have to remember to have him join in on some chokozetsu. Probably even try to get a dot or two of Court Goodwill (Fire Rat) if he travels back and forth often enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:47:28-07:00","id":964113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964109#post964109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you choose Tokyo to be the largest court/ population center for the Changelings/Lost and not a city like Beijing, Nanjing, or Shanghai? Chinese influence can be found in most of East Asia. Also, the Japan is dealing with a worse population decline than any other country in East Asia. It's not that I disapprove of Tokyo being the biggest metropolitan center for Changelings, but I am curious to see if you use some historical event to explain this like China's Great Leap Forward, the Cultural Revolution, or even the Bamboo curtain?</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to avoid crediting supernatural stories for sensitive cultural events, and the other way around. <br /> <br /> The reason it's the biggest population is because it's the biggest in scope. It literally encompasses over 100 million people. Most Freeholds are only a single city. Honshu is unique in that it's a massive kingdom spanning numerous major cities. <br /> <br /> It's not just Tokyo. Not even remotely. It's also Osaka. Kyoto. And MANY other cities. Honshu is massive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:51:33-07:00","id":964115,"title":"","content":"Do you plan to explore what the Courts in China are like? I am really eager to see if you create a court based on Journey to the West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:52:25-07:00","id":964116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964115#post964115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you plan to explore what the Courts in China are like? I am really eager to see if you create a court based on Journey to the West.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the core book. But, if I have space in a supplement, that's ABSOLUTELY a possibility. I don't know QUITE as much about China since I don't live there or know the language, but I did study it a bit in college.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:54:01-07:00","id":964118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964115#post964115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you plan to explore what the Courts in China are like? I am really eager to see if you create a court based on Journey to the West.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do have one canonical set of Chinese Courts in the Directional Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:55:05-07:00","id":964120,"title":"","content":"Whelp. Gonna have to use Tokyo in my next chronicle. No excuses anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T00:24:05-07:00","id":964135,"title":"","content":"Also, that bit about the Flamesiren with vampire lovers licking her blood off the floor in public might just be the most Chronicles of Darkness thing I've ever read, and it is glorious. It's weird and kinky and creepy, and there's, like, a whole <i>story </i>in that image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T00:25:06-07:00","id":964136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964135#post964135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, that bit about the Flamesiren with vampire lovers licking her blood off the floor in public might just be the most Chronicles of Darkness thing I've ever read, and it is glorious. It's weird and kinky and creepy, and there's, like, a whole <i>story </i>in that image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I'm particularly fond of that part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T02:57:35-07:00","id":964168,"title":"","content":"I feel a bit thick, but are the Gods and Otodo supposed to be something I recognize, but seen through a different lens? I'm struggling to think of any connections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T02:59:13-07:00","id":964169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964168#post964168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel a bit thick, but are the Gods and Otodo supposed to be something I recognize, but seen through a different lens? I'm struggling to think of any connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Otodo are explicitly mentioned in Dark Eras. They're an offshoot of the Lucifuge. <br /> <br /> The gods... Let me see if anyone else figures it out first. I want to let people play the guessing game a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:05:38-07:00","id":964173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964169#post964169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gods... Let me see if anyone else figures it out first. I want to let people play the guessing game a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption is mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:10:42-07:00","id":964178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964169#post964169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gods... Let me see if anyone else figures it out first. I want to let people play the guessing game a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly the Arisen as interpreted through Lost rumour?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:24:47-07:00","id":964235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964169#post964169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gods... Let me see if anyone else figures it out first. I want to let people play the guessing game a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964173#post964173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My assumption is mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. Mummies are worshiped by cults as gods. They're ancient beings. They're &quot;reborn&quot; again and again down the line, and they certainly do play the part of kings and queens throughout their history.<br /> <br /> Anyways, about the actual meat of the freehold. I do love the Moon Princess legend, though I am a bit sad we don't have a Jeweled Branch Court. I do find it a bit odd at the red tape involved - how many changelings must there be to support such a massive beaurocracy? Hundreds? Thousands? A million? More than anything, I feel like I can't quite grasp the scope of this freehold, and that's throwing me off. What made you decide to do Honshu as a whole instead of a single city?<br /> <br /> The Courts... honestly, I'm less than impressed with the Courts. I feel like they're rather shallow - an umbrella group of rebels and malcontents, traditional conservatives, and buddhist ascetics, as if you can paint those with a single brush each. I'm not feeling anything approaching depth to them. They're just kind of... there. They have no relationship to the larger freehold or its three factions, no roles to play, I'm not getting a sense of organization, I don't see how this relates to finding a new home, and I just don't get a feeling of any kind of personality. I get the feeling that they're unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I like the Leadership Council and Envoys, both of which are fun. I find that the best part of this writeup is the descriptions of the Envoys, which are beautifully done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:32:48-07:00","id":964238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964235#post964235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Mummies are worshiped by cults as gods. They're ancient beings. They're &quot;reborn&quot; again and again down the line, and they certainly do play the part of kings and queens throughout their history.<br /> <br /> Anyways, about the actual meat of the freehold. I do love the Moon Princess legend, though I am a bit sad we don't have a Jeweled Branch Court. I do find it a bit odd at the red tape involved - how many changelings must there be to support such a massive beaurocracy? Hundreds? Thousands? A million? More than anything, I feel like I can't quite grasp the scope of this freehold, and that's throwing me off. What made you decide to do Honshu as a whole instead of a single city?<br /> <br /> The Courts... honestly, I'm less than impressed with the Courts. I feel like they're rather shallow - an umbrella group of rebels and malcontents, traditional conservatives, and buddhist ascetics, as if you can paint those with a single brush each. I'm not feeling anything approaching depth to them. They're just kind of... there. They have no relationship to the larger freehold or its three factions, no roles to play, I'm not getting a sense of organization, I don't see how this relates to finding a new home, and I just don't get a feeling of any kind of personality. I get the feeling that they're unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I like the Leadership Council and Envoys, both of which are fun. I find that the best part of this writeup is the descriptions of the Envoys, which are beautifully done.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Envoys are really the focal point of the setting, that's why they got the bulk of the word count there.<br /> <br /> And yes, it's mummies. Maybe other stuff. But definitely mummies. I'd love to get to do a little treatment of Tokyo for Mummy. But, I don't know how likely that is. So, best I can do is seed little bits about the few that might be there.<br /> <br /> Jeweled Branch Court would make a great focus for a Dark Era...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 09-06-2016, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:10:14-07:00","id":964264,"title":"","content":"I love the write-up. I particularly like how you hint at a unique flavor of some of the Other societies - like the fact that most Sin-Eaters become so willingly. A question though: Don't &quot;Envoys to the Others&quot; and &quot;Emissary to the Others&quot; get confusing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964169#post964169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gods... Let me see if anyone else figures it out first. I want to let people play the guessing game a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been established that Gods are Mummies, but the part about rebirth into human bodies eats at me. Are they Deceived? Or even worse... Shuankhsen?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Rest of our Lives</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her role in the kingdom is that of a cornerstone. For the freehold to fall to the Gentry, she has to be wooed away. The Other must enter the kingdom, and vie for her hand in marriage. She must pose a (seemingly impossible) challenge to the would-be suitor, and the suitor conducts the task. If she agrees to the courtship, the whole kingdom falls apart, and the floodgates open to alien monstrosities.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something I can't infer from the text. What happens if a suitor succeeds?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Rest of our Lives</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an Approach, the Court of the Fire Rat prohibits repeat performances. Attacking the freehold in the same way twice simply does not work; one must try new things to oppose the moon princess.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why Rita Repulsa never uses the same monster twice.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:40:40-07:00","id":964282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964264#post964264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been established that Gods are Mummies, but the part about rebirth into human bodies eats at me. Are they Deceived? Or even worse... Shuankhsen?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probable that they have a stable method of being Twice-Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:51:15-07:00","id":964291,"title":"","content":"I love the fairy tale feel the Moon Princess and her impossible tasks for the Gentry gives off.<br /> <br /> I feel like the courts' emotions of choice are harder to feed from than the seasonal courts (the fire rats seem to have it easiest), and honestly I wouldn't even consider 'conformity' or 'tradition' emotions.<br /> <br /> The Envoys are great. Echoing the Eiko Furata love.<br /> <br /> Bit surprised that spirits and ghosts don't get envoys \u2013 I've always thought of them as more commonplace than some of the rarer things that have gotten envoys, but I suppose ghosts probably fall under the umbrella of 'the Dead', even if the lion's share of the wordcount goes to Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> For the Envoy to Fae, I'm guessing... fetches, goblins/hobs, fae-touched, and Gentry (I feel like I must be forgetting something here...) all fall under the umbrella, but other changelings \u2013 even those from outside the freehold \u2013 do not?<br /> <br /> Envoy to Humans, non-Otodo hunters and the Hototogisu, but obviously it wouldn't grant bonus dice to Social actions with just any human...<br /> <br /> Glad to get hints of what a Demon Tokyo would look like. Hopefully we'll get to see that, one day, along with the other gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:16:08-07:00","id":964302,"title":"","content":"Personally I suspect Spirits might fall under Gods. <br /> <br /> Anyway, really cool! By the by, do you have a concept for what the two lost Courts were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:24:00-07:00","id":964304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964264#post964264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the write-up. I particularly like how you hint at a unique flavor of some of the Other societies - like the fact that most Sin-Eaters become so willingly. A question though: Don't &quot;Envoys to the Others&quot; and &quot;Emissary to the Others&quot; get confusing?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a minor editing issue. I'll fix it for homogeneity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964264#post964264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been established that Gods are Mummies, but the part about rebirth into human bodies eats at me. Are they Deceived? Or even worse... Shuankhsen?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964264#post964264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something I can't infer from the text. What happens if a suitor succeeds?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also a really good question. It's never happened. But probably, the freehold would collapse, since the Moon Princess married an Other. It'd be like cats and dogs in the streets or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964264#post964264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why Rita Repulsa never uses the same monster twice.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>GOOD CATCH. Very minor Super Sentai reference. I wasn't expecting anyone to get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:26:53-07:00","id":964308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>indarkestknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964291#post964291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bit surprised that spirits and ghosts don't get envoys \u2013 I've always thought of them as more commonplace than some of the rarer things that have gotten envoys, but I suppose ghosts probably fall under the umbrella of 'the Dead', even if the lion's share of the wordcount goes to Sin-Eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts are really too simple to get an envoy. At least in the capacity the Lost can interact with them, they don't have big formal organizations. Most are just sort of echoes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>indarkestknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964291#post964291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Envoy to Fae, I'm guessing... fetches, goblins/hobs, fae-touched, and Gentry (I feel like I must be forgetting something here...) all fall under the umbrella, but other changelings \u2013 even those from outside the freehold \u2013 do not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Other Lost don't get a diplomat. They'd just have to deal with the Courts. Welcome to the bureaucratic nightmare of being a foreigner. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>indarkestknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964291#post964291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Envoy to Humans, non-Otodo hunters and the Hototogisu, but obviously it wouldn't grant bonus dice to Social actions with just any human...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. The implication is only humans who are clued in. I might clarify. But I'm not sure it's necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>indarkestknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964291#post964291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to get hints of what a Demon Tokyo would look like. Hopefully we'll get to see that, one day, along with the other gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd LOVE to do Demon Tokyo.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:27:37-07:00","id":964309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964302#post964302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I suspect Spirits might fall under Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, yeah. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964302#post964302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, really cool! By the by, do you have a concept for what the two lost Courts were?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have very, very loose ideas. I may fuss with them a little. I wanted to leave room for a potential Dark Era to pitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:09:50-07:00","id":964323,"title":"","content":"I like that there are so many story hooks, all the different Envoys are great for crossover hooks, The Defence force and Envoy to the Fae are great for more Changeling focused stories. And the courts have their own internal stories, but also provide the seeds of a story about change vs. tradition vs. harmony/balance.<br /> <br /> The Japan Freehold seems unusually stable and peaceful for a freehold, in large part because of the Envoys, but also that it has such a large population that is so well organized.<br /> <br /> Just a couple of questions however, to access a Court Emotion Contract and its special contract, do you have to be a Member of the Court or can you gain access with the Court Goodwill Merit? <br /> <br /> And can you have Court Good will merit with Courts outside your own, like having Goodwill \u2022\u2022\u2022 with the Jade Court, Seelie Court, Ash Court, Summer Court, Fire Rat Court, Copper Court?<br /> <br /> And lastly if Tailspinning is a Court Contract for all Courts, why isn't it just a general Contract, instead of a Court Contract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:17:24-07:00","id":964329,"title":"","content":"Travis Stoute says Ghosts are people, but rank 1 ghosts are on a hellish out repeat. Still I'd assume that they'd fall under the purview of the Envoy of the Dead, because Sin Eaters are part ghost and because ghosts are well dead. Same with the Underworld, but not Duat.<br /> <br /> I can see Deviants falling under a mix of Human Envoy (the ones that work for powerful corporations) and Envoy to the Others (rogue Deviants, weird cult made Deviants, and self made Deviants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:48:47-07:00","id":964346,"title":"","content":"How much do we have to pay for Mummy and Demon settings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:03:46-07:00","id":964352,"title":"","content":"I really like this writeup, definitely my favourite piece about the Japan setting so far. The Moon Princess is especially awesome, though one year terms feel exceedingly short. Just looking at comparisons to real life politics, it seems that would make long term change nearly impossible as anything that takes a year or more to realize will mostly get stuck unless several Princesses in a row work together closely. Which might be an intended outcome of the system, but makes bureaucratic adaption to changing circumstances much harder.<br /> <br /> I do believe the Envoys' writeups could be made to feel less... 'clean'. Especially compared to the Demon Storyteller guide's crossover chapter, where even these masters of information warfare clearly often had to base their information on lacklustre and often contradictory sources. In comparison envoys feel like they had their functions delinieated by someone who read the other lines' corebooks, not by a group of human(ish)s attempting to deal with a myriad monsters in a dark, sometimes weirdly inconsistent, and often terrifying universe.<br /> <br /> Also, and this might be based on an outdated idea of how the CofD is supposed to look, I do like the idea that the different core splats make up only a small part of the setting's supernatural activity, and most of it is by individual and unnamed horrors. It feels wrong that the Envoys map exactly onto the core splats + 1 for miscellaneous others, when IMO most Envoy activity should be concerned with any of the uncountable 'out-there's' of the the setting. I'd love if at least one or two Envoys were dedicated to societies of monsters that aren't one of the coresplats - either made up specifically for Japan, or a group that is mentioned in another line's books and that happens to be numerous enough in Japan to deserve their own Envoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:09:18-07:00","id":964358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964323#post964323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lastly if Tailspinning is a Court Contract for all Courts, why isn't it just a general Contract, instead of a Court Contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>Courtless would be my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:14:11-07:00","id":964361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964352#post964352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this writeup, definitely my favourite piece about the Japan setting so far. The Moon Princess is especially awesome, though one year terms feel exceedingly short. Just looking at comparisons to real life politics, it seems that would make long term change nearly impossible as anything that takes a year or more to realize will mostly get stuck unless several Princesses in a row work together closely. Which might be an intended outcome of the system, but makes bureaucratic adaption to changing circumstances much harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's an intended outcome from an OOC standpoint. The Fire Rats are an entire court (and probably absorbed one or both of the other courts) partly because it's so hard to actually push change through otherwise. And now that they've seen one of their own in the top job, and she's not making things that much different, they might want to start looking for other avenues to foment change. (Which is not at all an interpretation of the current American political climate at all. Nope. Totally.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:26:47-07:00","id":964372,"title":"","content":"really loved the writeup, and the Envoy section was really good! The bits about demons, mummies and sin eaters in Japan were really interesting, and I like it that the Azusa Miko has survived to modernity. Also, before that I've thought that I've got the impression that the japanese Ulgan were created independently, although that now it is pretty clear that it is not the case. Anyway, I really think that this writeup really use the full potential that Tokyo as a setting offers.<br /> <br /> Also- the Hero Guilds: are they under the Envoy for Humans or Myths? Does the Lost even have an Envoy for them, or perhaps they killed enough of them that they gave up on the idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:12:56-07:00","id":964408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964323#post964323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lastly if Tailspinning is a Court Contract for all Courts, why isn't it just a general Contract, instead of a Court Contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar reasons to the other universal Court affinity, for one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:36:47-07:00","id":964428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964408#post964408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar reasons to the other universal Court affinity, for one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, so its really Talespinning (insert court qaulity here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:54:03-07:00","id":964449,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've given the draft a really good look... and I am <i>loving</i> it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was really interested in reading more on the Yosei after the teaser they received in the Beast corebook. And this write-up did not disappoint at all. The whole society of the Japanese Lost was very unique and interesting, especially since the Envoys (my most favorite concept right above the Courts) makes their setting so crossover-friendly. Heck, it's pretty easy for a person to do a Beast/Changeling chronicle given how similar the two splats are organized in the country.<br /> <br /> On a related note, I am curious about what the other two Courts of the Freehold were... just as I am curious about the structure of the Edo Freehold mentioned in Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings are rather abundant in Edo. They organize in a court dedicated to Orihime, Amaterasu\u2019s weaver. They cling tightly to her principles of matchmaking, and for this reason have become fast friends with certain Hototogisu, and some of the Azusa Miko. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:12:16-07:00","id":964603,"title":"","content":"I just realized the unique advantage this court system has over others, to defeat the Freehold a True Fae has to successful seduce the Moon Princess and the True Fae has to acomplish the tasks set by her to do so.<br /> <br /> So one task could be to hunt down every enemy Loyalist in the Freehold, a task useful,but unlikely to be completed for other True Fae would send replacements before they're all gone.<br /> <br /> But it would still rid them of a bunch of Loyalists.<br /> <br /> So its way of making sure the True Fae are someone useful, but not too useful that they suceed and strike down the Freehold Bulkwark until the New Year (I assume things would start over with a new Moon Princess).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:36:50-07:00","id":964618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964329#post964329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Travis Stoute says Ghosts are people, but rank 1 ghosts are on a hellish out repeat. Still I'd assume that they'd fall under the purview of the Envoy of the Dead, because Sin Eaters are part ghost and because ghosts are well dead. Same with the Underworld, but not Duat.<br /> <br /> I can see Deviants falling under a mix of Human Envoy (the ones that work for powerful corporations) and Envoy to the Others (rogue Deviants, weird cult made Deviants, and self made Deviants).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't sure if Travis had said that publicly or not yet, so I didn't want to go there. They WOULD be covered by the same envoy. <br /> <br /> And I'd probably say Deviants fit under the Others. Not sure though. It depends on a few things that may or may not get said in Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:38:20-07:00","id":964620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964346#post964346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much do we have to pay for Mummy and Demon settings?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good question. I don't know? I can field the idea. See if it's a possibility, or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:42:43-07:00","id":964623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964352#post964352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this writeup, definitely my favourite piece about the Japan setting so far. The Moon Princess is especially awesome, though one year terms feel exceedingly short. Just looking at comparisons to real life politics, it seems that would make long term change nearly impossible as anything that takes a year or more to realize will mostly get stuck unless several Princesses in a row work together closely. Which might be an intended outcome of the system, but makes bureaucratic adaption to changing circumstances much harder.<br /> <br /> I do believe the Envoys' writeups could be made to feel less... 'clean'. Especially compared to the Demon Storyteller guide's crossover chapter, where even these masters of information warfare clearly often had to base their information on lacklustre and often contradictory sources. In comparison envoys feel like they had their functions delinieated by someone who read the other lines' corebooks, not by a group of human(ish)s attempting to deal with a myriad monsters in a dark, sometimes weirdly inconsistent, and often terrifying universe.<br /> <br /> Also, and this might be based on an outdated idea of how the CofD is supposed to look, I do like the idea that the different core splats make up only a small part of the setting's supernatural activity, and most of it is by individual and unnamed horrors. It feels wrong that the Envoys map exactly onto the core splats + 1 for miscellaneous others, when IMO most Envoy activity should be concerned with any of the uncountable 'out-there's' of the the setting. I'd love if at least one or two Envoys were dedicated to societies of monsters that aren't one of the coresplats - either made up specifically for Japan, or a group that is mentioned in another line's books and that happens to be numerous enough in Japan to deserve their own Envoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally like the idea. It's one reason why the Otodo are considered their own thing. They're NOT covered by the same diplomat as other Hunter characters, for example. But if I were to do something completely different, I feel like I'd owe at least some context. Not saying I won't when I pass for the final revisions. But, it depends on a few factors. <br /> <br /> And yes, the frustrating standstill of annual change is absolutely intended. It's a form of inborn conflict I expect will come up in play for some groups. <br /> <br /> It is a bit &quot;clean&quot;. That's intended. People are deeply in each others' business in this area. Secrets don't go too deep. It's not that everyone knows everything. But the Lost are a dominant group, and their diplomats are very knowledgeable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:44:22-07:00","id":964624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964361#post964361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's an intended outcome from an OOC standpoint. The Fire Rats are an entire court (and probably absorbed one or both of the other courts) partly because it's so hard to actually push change through otherwise. And now that they've seen one of their own in the top job, and she's not making things that much different, they might want to start looking for other avenues to foment change. (Which is not at all an interpretation of the current American political climate at all. Nope. Totally.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I think maybe some of the Dragons Jewels and Begging Bowls are secretly super thankful the Fire Rats exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:47:54-07:00","id":964627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964372#post964372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">really loved the writeup, and the Envoy section was really good! The bits about demons, mummies and sin eaters in Japan were really interesting, and I like it that the Azusa Miko has survived to modernity. Also, before that I've thought that I've got the impression that the japanese Ulgan were created independently, although that now it is pretty clear that it is not the case. Anyway, I really think that this writeup really use the full potential that Tokyo as a setting offers.<br /> <br /> Also- the Hero Guilds: are they under the Envoy for Humans or Myths? Does the Lost even have an Envoy for them, or perhaps they killed enough of them that they gave up on the idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wanted to do something with the Azusa Miko and Geist. So, I made them core to the history of the setting in Geist 2e. That history's a little more focused, and hits hard on a single event/period. <br /> <br /> I'd say Hero Guilds would fall under humans, but I'm not sure that they really interact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:57:59-07:00","id":964634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964449#post964449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've given the draft a really good look... and I am <i>loving</i> it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was really interested in reading more on the Yosei after the teaser they received in the Beast corebook. And this write-up did not disappoint at all. The whole society of the Japanese Lost was very unique and interesting, especially since the Envoys (my most favorite concept right above the Courts) makes their setting so crossover-friendly. Heck, it's pretty easy for a person to do a Beast/Changeling chronicle given how similar the two splats are organized in the country.<br /> <br /> On a related note, I am curious about what the other two Courts of the Freehold were... just as I am curious about the structure of the Edo Freehold mentioned in Dark Eras.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Jeweled Branch from Horai<br /> The Cowry Shell born of a Swallow<br /> <br /> I didn't give them too much thought, because I didn't want to fall in love with them if I didn't have the place to put them. I also try to give myself a little wiggle room for other potential books. So like, these two would be great for a Dark Era. <br /> <br /> And the Orihime Court was Edo-specific, it died off. It was all about weaving new stories, and building a new century. You'll find some minor hints about this in Geist 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:00:32-07:00","id":964636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964603#post964603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized the unique advantage this court system has over others, to defeat the Freehold a True Fae has to successful seduce the Moon Princess and the True Fae has to acomplish the tasks set by her to do so.<br /> <br /> So one task could be to hunt down every enemy Loyalist in the Freehold, a task useful,but unlikely to be completed for other True Fae would send replacements before they're all gone.<br /> <br /> But it would still rid them of a bunch of Loyalists.<br /> <br /> So its way of making sure the True Fae are someone useful, but not too useful that they suceed and strike down the Freehold Bulkwark until the New Year (I assume things would start over with a new Moon Princess).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and the Fae in question has to go through the diplomat to the Fae first, who screens them. So it's a rigorous process. And with the Court Approaches, there's even a massive layer of additional defense laid down. They can't use the same methods twice. They can't use but a fraction of their resources. And they have to actively engage Freehold defenses. And for this situation, those Freehold defenses are a literal army.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:27:48-07:00","id":964656,"title":"","content":"There are some interesting implications about how bulwarks work here.<br /> <br /> I wonder what one of the Gentry would have to offer the Moon Princess to get her to accept a proposal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:37:01-07:00","id":964663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964620#post964620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good question. I don't know? I can field the idea. See if it's a possibility, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>God, please don't make me wait until 2018/2019 for Mummy Tokyo. Demon Tokyo might actually need to be a standalone little thing unless there's some new supplements hiding on the horizon for that line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:57:59-07:00","id":964679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964656#post964656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some interesting implications about how bulwarks work here.<br /> <br /> I wonder what one of the Gentry would have to offer the Moon Princess to get her to accept a proposal?</div> </div> </div> </div>And, even more curiously, why haven't any managed so far? <br /> <br /> *Dramatic chord progression*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T20:23:17-07:00","id":964745,"title":"","content":"Oh, since people asked and it was fresh in my mind: <br /> <br /> The Lost Courts<br /> Two other Courts faded with the times. The first was the Cowry Shells, named after the Cowry Shell Born of Swallows. The second was the Jeweled Branches, named after the Jeweled Branch from Horai. These were the other two tasks given to suitors by Kaguya Hime in the Tale of the Bamboo Cutter.<br /> The Jeweled Branches were a highly animistic, spiritual group. They dealt with ghosts and the natural spirits. They never really fit in with the freehold at large, and indeed many simply ceased to participate or fled the region some time in the late 17<sup>th</sup> century, citing disgust with a curse the Lost placed on the dead of Honshu.<br /> The Cowry Shells represented decadence and wealth. They believed themselves natural nobility, deserving of praise and gifts. The Court existed largely to perpetuate itself; members selectively recruited those who could bring further riches into the order. They embedded deep within aristocratic families. They fell out of prominence in the late part of the nineteenth century, shaken heavily by the changes during the Meiji Restoration. Then, after World War II, the last remaining members pledged allegiance to other Courts, overwhelmingly the Dragon\u2019s Jewels. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:01:21-07:00","id":964753,"title":"","content":"wait... so the Moon Princess Courts were around together with the Orihime Court? Well, that answers any question I've had about the time frame, and it does mirrors the idea of the real power being in the hands of the shogun instead of the emperor (I would assume that the Moon Princess would work as Amaterasu to the Court's Orihime or something. I'm half asleep, so I may be missing a few things :P )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:22:23-07:00","id":964761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964634#post964634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jeweled Branch from Horai<br /> The Cowry Shell born of a Swallow<br /> <br /> I didn't give them too much thought, because I didn't want to fall in love with them if I didn't have the place to put them. I also try to give myself a little wiggle room for other potential books. So like, these two would be great for a Dark Era.<br /> <br /> And the Orihime Court was Edo-specific, it died off. It was all about weaving new stories, and building a new century. You'll find some minor hints about this in Geist 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist 2E.... Okay, <i>that</i> is the biggest tidbit I've heard from the splat so far. <i>Now</i> I'm curious XD<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964745#post964745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, since people asked and it was fresh in my mind:<br /> <u><b>The Lost Courts</b></u><br /> Two other Courts faded with the times. The first was the Cowry Shells, named after the Cowry Shell Born of Swallows. The second was the Jeweled Branches, named after the Jeweled Branch from Horai. These were the other two tasks given to suitors by Kaguya Hime in the Tale of the Bamboo Cutter.<br /> <br /> The Jeweled Branches were a highly animistic, spiritual group. They dealt with ghosts and the natural spirits. They never really fit in with the freehold at large, and indeed many simply ceased to participate or fled the region some time in the late 17<sup>th</sup> century, citing disgust with a curse the Lost placed on the dead of Honshu.<br /> <br /> The Cowry Shells represented decadence and wealth. They believed themselves natural nobility, deserving of praise and gifts. The Court existed largely to perpetuate itself; members selectively recruited those who could bring further riches into the order. They embedded deep within aristocratic families. They fell out of prominence in the late part of the nineteenth century, shaken heavily by the changes during the Meiji Restoration. Then, after World War II, the last remaining members pledged allegiance to other Courts, overwhelmingly the Dragon\u2019s Jewels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, can I just say that I like these concepts for the two Lost Courts? Excuse me while I note these down for future ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:51:50-07:00","id":964780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964761#post964761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geist 2E.... Okay, <i>that</i> is the biggest tidbit I've heard from the splat so far. <i>Now</i> I'm curious XD<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. That's such a tiny little tidbit. The reference in Geist isn't really that explicit. But, if you read both, you should be able to connect the dots pretty easily. It's not like a super oblique reference or anything like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:54:03-07:00","id":964782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964753#post964753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait... so the Moon Princess Courts were around together with the Orihime Court? Well, that answers any question I've had about the time frame, and it does mirrors the idea of the real power being in the hands of the shogun instead of the emperor (I would assume that the Moon Princess would work as Amaterasu to the Court's Orihime or something. I'm half asleep, so I may be missing a few things :P )</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, it's mostly just a matter of the Orihime Court existing as its own very Edo thing, and the Moon Princess wasn't quite as established, and didn't really care. At this point, Edo was like the new kid in town. It was probably largely overlooked. They weren't as much separatist or anything like that, as they were just very self-interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:27:40-07:00","id":964851,"title":"","content":"I liked the Envoy and the basic freehold idea with the story and the rest. I really think the new system makes the game better and this is a good example of how interesting it can be. On the Geist forum, there are already requests for Geist Tokyo edition.<br /> <br /> There was actually a debate about ghosts, so yeah, the news has been broken (clarified really). I would guess the Envoy of the Dead deals with ghosts of low rank, or more likely has Sin-Eaters deal with them, and of the Others would mess around with the higher ranked ghosts and other nasty things from the Underworld, at least until they are identified. I imagine spirits is also split with Gods and Others.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it is a typo because of the dynamics of vampire, but you have three major organizations then go to conflict between two groups. If the wording is correct then I assume you mean the zaibatsu and they would conflict with another group. On the other hand there would be Hototogisu, zaibatsu and the Lance as the three. I'm not sure it is as clear as you would like. I know this isn't an editing session, but I think it is important conceptually to know if there would be overlap between Envoys. Otherwise they seem written so they would be very much separate in their official efforts.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the open knowledge is fine. They had centuries to develop the knowledge base and specifically set out to create diplomatic relations with other supers. It isn't the normal everyone to their corner and we will leave you alone as long as you leave us alone mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T03:46:06-07:00","id":964883,"title":"","content":"Huh. I really thought that the jeweled branch would be focusing on Hedge fruits and the like instead of ephemeral entities. Still, curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T04:11:44-07:00","id":964887,"title":"","content":"The Jeweled Branch could still be out there, beyond the Moon Princess' borders perhaps having turned into its own Freehold, splitting into 2 courts, one for spirits and one for ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T04:51:24-07:00","id":964895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964887#post964887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jeweled Branch could still be out there, beyond the Moon Princess' borders perhaps having turned into its own Freehold, splitting into 2 courts, one for spirits and one for ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Yosei Kingdom <i>is</i> confined to Honshu more or less. So maybe such a Freehold could be based in another region of Japan? Or even beyond it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:08:21-07:00","id":964998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964782#post964782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really, it's mostly just a matter of the Orihime Court existing as its own very Edo thing, and the Moon Princess wasn't quite as established, and didn't really care. At this point, Edo was like the new kid in town. It was probably largely overlooked. They weren't as much separatist or anything like that, as they were just very self-interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, that kills my &quot;Orihime has messed up/betrayed her people by letting the Gentry into the Freehold, having the Moon Princess to save the day, destroy her Court and erase her name from history&quot; idea I've had. Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:52:06-07:00","id":965339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964998#post964998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, that kills my &quot;Orihime has messed up/betrayed her people by letting the Gentry into the Freehold, having the Moon Princess to save the day, destroy her Court and erase her name from history&quot; idea I've had. Oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a really groovy idea. I dig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:54:22-07:00","id":965342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964895#post964895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Yosei Kingdom <i>is</i> confined to Honshu more or less. So maybe such a Freehold could be based in another region of Japan? Or even beyond it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see them perhaps spreading to Hokkaido, Shikoku, Kyushu, and Okinawa. Okinawa would actually offer some really cool aesthetic opportunities for a spinoff freehold. And Hokkaido would offer a lot of interesting implications with its climate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:13:25-07:00","id":965351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964352#post964352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels wrong that the Envoys map exactly onto the core splats + 1 for miscellaneous others, when IMO most Envoy activity should be concerned with any of the uncountable 'out-there's' of the the setting. I'd love if at least one or two Envoys were dedicated to societies of monsters that aren't one of the coresplats - either made up specifically for Japan, or a group that is mentioned in another line's books and that happens to be numerous enough in Japan to deserve their own Envoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was kinda thinking about this regarding the Gods, which are certainly mummies (or mostly mummies, but I'll get to that):<br /> <br /> Mummies spend most of 'their time' in <i>henet</i>, their death sleep. I don't imagine a huge amount of them being awake at any given point, not to the degree where an outsider splat would look at one or two and piece the puzzle together like, &quot;Yes, of course they must be part of a supernatural conspiracy with their own elaborate mythology, power sources, and six different social splats separate from the innumerable Horrors of the world of darkness.&quot; I feel like some of the 'non-major' splats, like blue book Horrors, might be more numerous and deserving of an Envoy than mummies, at least on a local/regional level like you suggest.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, think about it in the reverse. We know some groups stand out enough from the rest of their splat to receive their own Envoy (Otodo? Lucifuge guys), so maybe we can assume the Envoy of the Gods interacts with more than just mummies, which is what was suggested, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:19:35-07:00","id":965352,"title":"","content":"Like most others, I really enjoyed this writeup. Rife with story hooks both crossover and otherwise.<br /> <br /> I do have one little uncertainty though: the mention of the Hototogisu says the high number of Lost could easily beat them in open conflict. But it also implies the Vampires have high numbers, yet their struggle against the human organization is a big theme in their own writeup. Are the lost that much more populous, is it meant to more imply the Vampires AND Lost together would make short work, or is there something else that would make it easier for Changelings than Vampires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:42:12-07:00","id":965372,"title":"","content":"Very interesting and fairly unexpected write-up! The scope of the activities and membership of the freehold makes for a impressive picture, but I'm most struck by all the unique details on how the diverse supernatural groups of the region interact with the enjoys and each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-07-2016, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:45:28-07:00","id":965375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965352#post965352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like most others, I really enjoyed this writeup. Rife with story hooks both crossover and otherwise.<br /> <br /> I do have one little uncertainty though: the mention of the Hototogisu says the high number of Lost could easily beat them in open conflict. But it also implies the Vampires have high numbers, yet their struggle against the human organization is a big theme in their own writeup. Are the lost that much more populous, is it meant to more imply the Vampires AND Lost together would make short work, or is there something else that would make it easier for Changelings than Vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampires number in the hundreds. Perhaps a thousand. And vampires notoriously Don't Get Along That Well. There are upwards of 20,000 Lost, more or less all recognizing a central government. It's an order of magnitude thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:46:59-07:00","id":965376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965375#post965375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vampires number in the hundreds. Perhaps a thousand. And vampires notoriously Don't Get Along That Well. There are upwards of 20,000 Lost, more or less all recognizing a central government. It's an order of magnitude thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that definitely makes sense then. Thanks for satiating my curiosity!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:01:57-07:00","id":965412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=964998#post964998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, that kills my &amp;quot;Orihime has messed up/betrayed her people by letting the Gentry into the Freehold, having the Moon Princess to save the day, destroy her Court and erase her name from history&amp;quot; idea I've had. Oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965339#post965339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually a really groovy idea. I dig.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that. And I imagine that could be something that happens around the time of the Meiji Restoration? It seems appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:17:18-07:00","id":965418,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Moon Princess saving the day, this is literally a conversation I had with my wife Filamena regarding this chapter. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/Zx8KS\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/Zx8KS\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/Zx8KS\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/a/Zx8KS </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:18:34-07:00","id":965420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965342#post965342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see them perhaps spreading to Hokkaido, Shikoku, Kyushu, and Okinawa. Okinawa would actually offer some really cool aesthetic opportunities for a spinoff freehold. And Hokkaido would offer a lot of interesting implications with its climate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. A Kyushu-based freehold would probably be centered around Nagasaki. The ghosts and spirits that would have popped up there after the Bomb was dropped could very well be their biggest concern.<br /> <br /> As for Okinawa and Hokkaido, what sort of implications did you have in mind? Politically, I could see the Jeweled Branch sharing the former with regional Directional Courts from Taiwan and/or China but that's all I got so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 09-07-2016, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:23:01-07:00","id":965423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965420#post965420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. A Kyushu-based freehold would probably be centered around Nagasaki. The ghosts and spirits that would have popped up there after the Bomb was dropped could very well be their biggest concern.<br /> <br /> As for Okinawa and Hokkaido, what sort of implications did you have in mind? Politically, I could see the Jeweled Branch sharing the former with regional Directional Courts from Taiwan and/or China but that's all I got so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, religious practice in Okinawa is far different. Also, the US military influence there would be a significant thing. And for Hokkaido, the focus on cold would give it a feeling not dissimilar from classic Winter Court stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:03:24-07:00","id":965465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965339#post965339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a really groovy idea. I dig.</div> </div> </div> </div>something that has just occurred to me-<br /> <br /> The Moon Princess stop others through impossible marriage tasks. The Orihime Court are matchmakers. What if the Court's betrayal would be that Orihime helped one of the suitors with his task, making it that the Moon Princess has almost married with him? The question is, of course, what would make Orihime and/or her Court to make such betrayal..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:29:10-07:00","id":965478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965465#post965465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something that has just occurred to me-<br /> <br /> The Moon Princess stop others through impossible marriage tasks. The Orihime Court are matchmakers. What if the Court's betrayal would be that Orihime helped one of the suitors with his task, making it that the Moon Princess has almost married with him? The question is, of course, what would make Orihime and/or her Court to make such betrayal..</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be like a whole Dark Era's worth of content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:34:47-07:00","id":965481,"title":"","content":"David, any brief thoughts for someone possibly considering a Werewolf setting in the Meiji era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:01:26-07:00","id":965489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965481#post965481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David, any brief thoughts for someone possibly considering a Werewolf setting in the Meiji era?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. What part of the Meiji Jidai? The early part? The late part? What would your general theme be? What would you want to tap into and accomplish? What exactly would characters be doing, and why is that unique to your vision of the period? What unique options are available to players? What do you see as a primary focus of conflict and antagonism? Do you intend to tie it with any established setting ideas and events, such as the slow extinction of the Japanese Wolf? Do you want it to be a more general experience, or a highly focused snapshot of one aspect of the setting? Are there any existing splats and game concepts that can be refocused with just a little word count to say a lot about your piece of the world? What is the Hisil like? What do you expect the world and the Hisil to look like at the beginning of the chronicle, and how might that be different from the end of a chronicle? <br /> <br /> More specifically, do you intend on integrating the five provisions of the Gokajo no Goseimon and either commenting upon or adapting them to say something about your chronicle? Do you plan on using the exaltation of the zaibatsu in your story? How do you see the adoption of Western technology as influencing this setting? How about the Bank of Japan? During the 1870s, Japan brought in an unprecedented number of foreigners, bringing 3,000 skilled workers and teachers. How does this shift reflect in your setting? A major change we see is in the adoption of extensive telegraph lines and train systems, how does this matter for your stories? Coming off the end of the sakoku, a lot of Japanese felt depowered and overly influenced by foreign powers. How does this matter to your stories? <br /> <br /> That's basically the core of what I'd consider if I were writing a werewolf setting in the period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:44:02-07:00","id":965507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965489#post965489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno. What part of the Meiji Jidai? The early part? The late part? What would your general theme be? What would you want to tap into and accomplish? What exactly would characters be doing, and why is that unique to your vision of the period? What unique options are available to players? What do you see as a primary focus of conflict and antagonism? Do you intend to tie it with any established setting ideas and events, such as the slow extinction of the Japanese Wolf? Do you want it to be a more general experience, or a highly focused snapshot of one aspect of the setting? Are there any existing splats and game concepts that can be refocused with just a little word count to say a lot about your piece of the world? What is the Hisil like? What do you expect the world and the Hisil to look like at the beginning of the chronicle, and how might that be different from the end of a chronicle? <br /> <br /> More specifically, do you intend on integrating the five provisions of the Gokajo no Goseimon and either commenting upon or adapting them to say something about your chronicle? Do you plan on using the exaltation of the zaibatsu in your story? How do you see the adoption of Western technology as influencing this setting? How about the Bank of Japan? During the 1870s, Japan brought in an unprecedented number of foreigners, bringing 3,000 skilled workers and teachers. How does this shift reflect in your setting? A major change we see is in the adoption of extensive telegraph lines and train systems, how does this matter for your stories? Coming off the end of the sakoku, a lot of Japanese felt depowered and overly influenced by foreign powers. How does this matter to your stories? <br /> <br /> That's basically the core of what I'd consider if I were writing a werewolf setting in the period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't derail this thread any more past this post, but my general idea was the fall of traditional Japanese culture to foreign influence and rapid modernization definitely echoed to the Forsaken the death of Father Wolf at his children's hands; destroy something precious in order to adapt, or fall by the wayside. The abolishing of the samurai class and the extinction of the Japanese wolf likewise emphasize the old ways dying and threatening to take the Forsaken with them, and that's before the chaos in the Shadow resulting from the conflict between ancient, local spirits clashing with new spirits of strange ideologies and technologies. Do the Forsaken allow themselves to stagnate and be forgotten in the name of pride and tradition (and accept a fate as a dying breed of spiritual ronin) or do they abandon the past in order to be the fresh predators of tomorrow - or is there a balance to somehow be struck?<br /> <br /> Then there's the excuse to have black and white artwork of a Blood Talon that looks suspiciously like Toshiro Mifune, but that's hardly something I can be blamed for, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T23:45:55-07:00","id":965523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965478#post965478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be like a whole Dark Era's worth of content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you played <i>Tomb Raider</i> 2013? It's all about a bunch of students and researches getting trapped on a shipwreck island by the powers of a [Sun] queen. Someone in one of the WoD subforums was making their own little Yamatai Dark Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:38:34-07:00","id":965542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965523#post965523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you played <i>Tomb Raider</i> 2013? It's all about a bunch of students and researches getting trapped on a shipwreck island by the powers of a [Sun] queen. Someone in one of the WoD subforums was making their own little Yamatai Dark Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have. I more or less dug it, but I thought the underground cave of thousands of bodies was goofy as fuck, and I thought it was very dissonant to see her respond to like her eighth murder with this visceral revulsion, but her 1st through 7th were fine, and her 9th through 86,549th were all groovy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:39:51-07:00","id":965543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965507#post965507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I won't derail this thread any more past this post, but my general idea was the fall of traditional Japanese culture to foreign influence and rapid modernization definitely echoed to the Forsaken the death of Father Wolf at his children's hands; destroy something precious in order to adapt, or fall by the wayside. The abolishing of the samurai class and the extinction of the Japanese wolf likewise emphasize the old ways dying and threatening to take the Forsaken with them, and that's before the chaos in the Shadow resulting from the conflict between ancient, local spirits clashing with new spirits of strange ideologies and technologies. Do the Forsaken allow themselves to stagnate and be forgotten in the name of pride and tradition (and accept a fate as a dying breed of spiritual ronin) or do they abandon the past in order to be the fresh predators of tomorrow - or is there a balance to somehow be struck?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty cool. I'd play a game like that. Although by that point, samurai are basically a joke anyway. Society was just formally recognizing what was long-since acknowledged. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965507#post965507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there's the excuse to have black and white artwork of a Blood Talon that looks suspiciously like Toshiro Mifune, but that's hardly something I can be blamed for, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I support this message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:54:51-07:00","id":965546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965543#post965543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds pretty cool. I'd play a game like that. Although by that point, samurai are basically a joke anyway. Society was just formally recognizing what was long-since acknowledged.<br /> <br /> I support this message.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Your validation has made my night.<br /> <br /> Back vaguely on topic, how many Gods/Mummies do you really think are even in Tokyo? Maho Suzuki doesnt't seem like she has that much work on her plate unless a disproportionate number of ancient Egyptian mortals have found their way into Japan over the long course of history or her purview is significantly wider than it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T01:00:04-07:00","id":965547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965546#post965546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! Your validation has made my night.<br /> <br /> Back vaguely on topic, how many Gods/Mummies do you really think are even in Tokyo? Maho Suzuki doesnt't seem like she has that much work on her plate unless a disproportionate number of ancient Egyptian mortals have found their way into Japan over the long course of history or her purview is significantly wider than it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very, very few. Often none.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T01:32:11-07:00","id":965555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965523#post965523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you played <i>Tomb Raider</i> 2013? It's all about a bunch of students and researches getting trapped on a shipwreck island by the powers of a [Sun] queen. Someone in one of the WoD subforums was making their own little Yamatai Dark Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I game mastered a chronicle in Yamatai with the 1st edition. Four players, they chose two werewolves and two vampires.<br /> <br /> An Irraka Blod Talon, an ex-militar friend of Roth, asked to go to the expedition by him. A Cahalith Master of Iron that works as private investigator, hired by the family Nishimura to protect her daughter from the &quot;bad influence&quot; of Lara. A Gangrel (Dead Wolves bloodline) of the Ordo Dracul, sended by his sire to assure that the monetary inversion he made to the expedition comes to fruit. A Daeva (Septimi bloodline) Carthian, sended by the Movement to investigate why the Invictus and the Ordo Dracul invested so much money on the expedition, he and Grim were close friends in the second world war and now he pretends to be his own grand son (&quot;oh my, you are the live image of your grandfather!!&quot;, Grim said XD)<br /> <br /> The chronicle was part supernatural investigation (the werewolves rapidly noticed that the isle was full of all kind of aggressive spirits and that something were very wrong there), survival and combat. The Solari may be are humans, but they have witnessed lots of strange things and are a little nuts (this is the reason I made the effects of Lunacy less potent) and are armed to the teeth. They learned quickly that stealth, cover and discretion were required.<br /> <br /> I also house ruled that the vamps could actuate at daytime, at the cost of 1 vitae and capping their dices to their humanity level.<br /> <br /> It was a very funny experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 09-08-2016, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:19:04-07:00","id":965591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965542#post965542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have. I more or less dug it, but I thought the underground cave of thousands of bodies was goofy as fuck, and I thought it was very dissonant to see her respond to like her eighth murder with this visceral revulsion, but her 1st through 7th were fine, and her 9th through 86,549th were all groovy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll put up with a bit of ludonarrative dissonance for a protagonist that actually visceral revulsion with their first murders, even if they become a princess rescuing sociopath in the span of, like, two days. That and <i>Far Cry 3</i> are the only games I've played recently where the protagonist was like... &quot;I just killed someone, that's messed up&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965543#post965543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although by that point, samurai are basically a joke anyway. Society was just formally recognizing what was long-since acknowledged.</div> </div> </div> </div>The aristocracy are always a joke. #EatTheRich<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12340_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12340\" data-vbnamecard=\"12340\">dourden</a> So essentially an alternate WoD version of the game? The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\">forum post in question</a> was more of a Dark Era thing, which is why I'd been asking about it in the context of historical stuff.<br /> Also, was this 1e? Vamps actually can ignore the Daysleep. I think it's Stamina+Resolve.<br /> <br /> But I'm sort of dragging the conversation away from Changeling, so time to fix that and give my detailed thoughts:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Isn't Yosei the Japanese term for a faerie?<br /> I like the story, but between this and Toronto, I'm not sure how the Bulwark works. Here is the Bulwark the tithe of gold (how do the motleys all manage to keep that consistent? What happens if someone isn't in a Motley? What happens if a few Motleys don't/can't pay?) or is it the need to woo the princess? Obviously the court falls if Yukihime gets swept off her feet, but what about the minor things? What happens if the princess doesn't choose a successor and just goes &quot;yeah, I have another year&quot;, or people can't pay the gold tithe (which I assume is getting sold back to mortal society to finance the Freehold)? Does everything crumble instantly or just sort of gradually get worse?<br /> This is all really more to do with Freeholds as a whole more than Honshu specifically. Are Approaches for the <i>entire Freehold</i>, or simply members of the Courts with that level of mantle? The Fire Rat part says their Approach prevents attacking the Freehold the same way twice, for instance; is that the entire freehold, or individual members? Can two Huntsmen attack the same way, or is it never the same way twice period? I'm not actually sure what the Dragon's Jewel Approach means. No sneaking passed walls, you've got to bust them down? Or are they intentionally ambiguous for the ST to decide?<br /> Aside from Shit Happening\u2122, one of the reasons I didn't run anything for the Playtest is because I couldn't wrap my head around how the Bulwark works or how it starts to fail.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel you've done a disservice telling us the Courts are based on the impossible tasks, but not actually telling us <i>what</i> the impossible tasks were. I mean, a Dragon's Jewel is pretty obvious, and the asceticism thing could just be a challenge to be poor, but where does setting a rat on fire come into play?<br /> <br /> Isn't 12 Ulgan a bit much for one place, especially if there are only about 100 or so Promethean at a time? What about non-Ulgan? And they all seem implied to be on the Refinement of Argentum.<br /> I will say I'm curious about this Geist bit here. It's been brought up in the Geist thread (and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> says you can't share more yet), but I'm curious how all the Sin-eaters in Honshu undertake this pilgrimage. Wouldn't that make them all the same Threshold?<br /> Also, Angels being referred to as Shito? Is that a reference I see? Likewise, is &quot;alternate revenue stream&quot; another one? <br /> <br /> And, since no one else has, <i>mechanical criticisms</i>, which I know you just love:<br /> For <b>Lashout</b>, the Darkling option should say dots in the Contract, not Merit.<br /> Worth noting is that the Fairest option actually becomes <i>less</i> useful as you take dots in the Merit.<br /> <br /> For <b>Hoard</b>, I hate the contract on general principle, because I hate the Availability subsystem. Neat concept, though. I always love rabbit-from-a-hat powers.<br /> Also, why Survival instead of, say, Larceny, or something more befitting the old traditionalists, like Socialize or Politics?<br /> What if I want to use the Beast version to pull a grubby little monster out of the bag without having to choose to take a Dramatic Failure? Also, might I suggest stating the grubby little monster's stats? A Retainer with health of [dots]+2?<br /> <br /> For <b>Calm Before Storms</b>, a few questions/clarifications: How does the Fairest version benefit, since the Social Maneuvering system doesn't cover initiative based actions? And what does &quot;turn an Extended action into an Instant Action&quot; mean? Make the Extended rolls each turn, or instead of making multiple rolls, roll a single dice pool? What are the limitations on that? Will I still need multiple successes to, say, pick a lock? <br /> <br /> <b>Envoy to the Others</b> is rather strong. +3 flat Social bonus, with the additional benefit of allowing the purchase of Social Merits related to other supernatural groups? It's only limited to \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, but an Envoy with Status \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf with the Invictus has a +6 bonus to social rolls with the Invictus, while someone with Status (Invictus) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf only has +5, though I suppose they don't get any of the other benefits of Status \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf; still, something to think about.<br /> <br /> The notion of the YSDF being essentially mercenaries is great, but 300 of them? That's quite a large number, way more than the seemingly lowballed number of Vampires in Tokyo proper, which if I recall was only 200 for the whole city of 13,620,000 people. And that's only a fraction of Honshu's Lost. I mean, I know Honshu total has 103m+ people, but I can never get a head for how many people in a given area are part of a supernatural type. Either way, the notion of people potentially having faerie bodyguards is a pretty good plothook for non-Changeling chronicles.<br /> <br /> As for Gotenba, as someone else asked... what about all the <i>gaijin </i>changeling climbing the mountain with the tourists?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Anyway. Those are my thoughts/questions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:53:43-07:00","id":965643,"title":"","content":"If the Moon Princess gets swept off her feet, the Freehold won't fall because her daughter from a thousand years in the future will travel back in time to save the day after she transforms into Chibi Moon Princess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, regarding the story the part about the challenges is<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Princess Moonlight then sent word to the First Knight that she requested him to bring her the stone bowl which had belonged to Buddha in India.<br /> <br /> The Second Knight was asked to go to the Mountain of Horai, said to be situated in the Eastern Sea, and to bring her a branch of the wonderful tree that grew on its summit. The roots of this tree were of silver, the trunk of gold, and the branches bore as fruit white jewels.<br /> <br /> The Third Knight was told to go to China and search for the fire-rat and to bring her its skin.<br /> <br /> The Fourth Knight was told to search for the dragon that carried on its head the stone radiating five colors and to bring the stone to her.<br /> <br /> The Fifth Knight was to find the swallow which carried a shell in its stomach and to bring the shell to her </div> </div> </div>You can read the whole story <a href=\"http://etc.usf.edu/lit2go/72/japanese-fairy-tales/4834/the-bamboo-cutter-and-the-moon-child/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> by downloading Passage PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-08-2016, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:14:01-07:00","id":965653,"title":"","content":"Super good notes. Thank you so much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll put up with a bit of ludonarrative dissonance for a protagonist that actually visceral revulsion with their first murders, even if they become a princess rescuing sociopath in the span of, like, two days. That and <i>Far Cry 3</i> are the only games I've played recently where the protagonist was like... &quot;I just killed someone, that's messed up&quot;.<br /> The aristocracy are always a joke. #EatTheRich</div> </div> </div> </div>#EatTheRich indeed. I think we can all agree on that. <br /> <br /> But yeah. It's a great game. I think Rhianna Pratchett is brilliant, and not just because she told me she's a huge fan. But that's a big part of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Yosei the Japanese term for a faerie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The breakaway there is an internal note that slipped through. Whoops. It happens when I export to PDF sometimes. Armory: Reloaded has a few of those artifacts, but much funnier. <br /> <br /> It was a pun. For my own reference. But yes, it's a word for fairy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the story, but between this and Toronto, I'm not sure how the Bulwark works. Here is the Bulwark the tithe of gold (how do the motleys all manage to keep that consistent? What happens if someone isn't in a Motley? What happens if a few Motleys don't/can't pay?) or is it the need to woo the princess? Obviously the court falls if Yukihime gets swept off her feet, but what about the minor things? What happens if the princess doesn't choose a successor and just goes &quot;yeah, I have another year&quot;, or people can't pay the gold tithe (which I assume is getting sold back to mortal society to finance the Freehold)? Does everything crumble instantly or just sort of gradually get worse?<br /> This is all really more to do with Freeholds as a whole more than Honshu specifically. Are Approaches for the <i>entire Freehold</i>, or simply members of the Courts with that level of mantle? The Fire Rat part says their Approach prevents attacking the Freehold the same way twice, for instance; is that the entire freehold, or individual members? Can two Huntsmen attack the same way, or is it never the same way twice period? I'm not actually sure what the Dragon's Jewel Approach means. No sneaking passed walls, you've got to bust them down? Or are they intentionally ambiguous for the ST to decide?<br /> Aside from Shit Happening\u2122, one of the reasons I didn't run anything for the Playtest is because I couldn't wrap my head around how the Bulwark works or how it starts to fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to clarify that in the final version of the bulwark stuff. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I feel you've done a disservice telling us the Courts are based on the impossible tasks, but not actually telling us <i>what</i> the impossible tasks were. I mean, a Dragon's Jewel is pretty obvious, and the asceticism thing could just be a challenge to be poor, but where does setting a rat on fire come into play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh shit. That's me assuming people know an old story just because I know it. Duh. I'll expound a little bit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't 12 Ulgan a bit much for one place, especially if there are only about 100 or so Promethean at a time? What about non-Ulgan? And they all seem implied to be on the Refinement of Argentum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know Matt put hard numbers in Promethean 2E. I THOUGHT we weren't doing that, but I haven't read the whole final product yet. That said, this is from Promethean Tokyo: <br /> <br /> &quot;The Created have extensive history in the Tokyo region. By far, Ulgan are the most common Prometheans in the area. Tokyo\u2019s Riven come from a pre-Shinto ritual from the J\u014dmon period of Japanese history. The practice continued across nearly 10,000 years. Other Lineages didn\u2019t come into play in the region until the 17<sup>th</sup> century, and even then only occur in unsubstantiated stories. It wasn\u2019t until the mid 19<sup>th</sup> century, when Japan opened its shores to the outside world, that other Created would visit in any number.<br /> The Created are never particularly common, but in the 21<sup>st</sup> century, Tokyo sees representation from most if not all major Lineages at a given time. The Ulgan still dominate numerically; two all-Ulgan Throngs reside in the Chiba and Saitama prefectures.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say I'm curious about this Geist bit here. It's been brought up in the Geist thread (and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> says you can't share more yet), but I'm curious how all the Sin-eaters in Honshu undertake this pilgrimage. Wouldn't that make them all the same Threshold?<br /> Also, Angels being referred to as Shito? Is that a reference I see? Likewise, is &quot;alternate revenue stream&quot; another one?</div> </div> </div> </div>A) You're working off incomplete, biased information. It doesn't mean what you think it means. <br /> <br /> B) Yes, it's a reference. Good catch. I put a similar reference, sometimes oblique, into each Tokyo piece. <br /> <br /> C) Yes, it's a reference. Good catch. I literally put a Leverage reference into most everything I do. Sometimes accidentally. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, since no one else has, <i>mechanical criticisms</i>, which I know you just love:</div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck yes. Thank you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b>Lashout</b>, the Darkling option should say dots in the Contract, not Merit.<br /> Worth noting is that the Fairest option actually becomes <i>less</i> useful as you take dots in the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, typo. It happens. <br /> <br /> On the Fairest thing, I think I'll be changing it so your rolled successes are what's compared. So if your attack rolls fewer than the attack you're countering, you can use their successes instead of yours. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b>Hoard</b>, I hate the contract on general principle, because I hate the Availability subsystem. Neat concept, though. I always love rabbit-from-a-hat powers.<br /> Also, why Survival instead of, say, Larceny, or something more befitting the old traditionalists, like Socialize or Politics?<br /> What if I want to use the Beast version to pull a grubby little monster out of the bag without having to choose to take a Dramatic Failure? Also, might I suggest stating the grubby little monster's stats? A Retainer with health of [dots]+2?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's okay. It hates you on principle, too. <br /> <br /> I actually agree on Larceny. I think I'll use that. I can't even remember why I went with Survival. I know I mulled it over a bit, and I remember having a reason, but whatever. <br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Beast:</b> You can opt to draw forth a monster as if you rolled a Dramatic Failure. If you pull a monster \u2013 even with Dramatic Failure, you can offer it simple, non-suicidal commands, one per dot in the Contract. <br /> <br /> And yeah, I'll do that for the stats. I need to keep it super simple, but that works well. I guess that's why I made those rules in the first place. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b>Calm Before Storms</b>, a few questions/clarifications: How does the Fairest version benefit, since the Social Maneuvering system doesn't cover initiative based actions? And what does &quot;turn an Extended action into an Instant Action&quot; mean? Make the Extended rolls each turn, or instead of making multiple rolls, roll a single dice pool? What are the limitations on that? Will I still need multiple successes to, say, pick a lock?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> You become more impressive as you weather the storm. Characters attempting to attack you or otherwise directly affect you during the waiting period must spend a point of Willpower per action.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Wizened:</b> You find shortcuts with your time spent. Turn an extended action into an instant action with this Contract. You need only roll once instead of multiple times. Add twice your Contract dots in successes to the single roll. You still need the normal required successes, but can accomplish the action in a single turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Envoy to the Others</b> is rather strong. +3 flat Social bonus, with the additional benefit of allowing the purchase of Social Merits related to other supernatural groups? It's only limited to \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, but an Envoy with Status \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf with the Invictus has a +6 bonus to social rolls with the Invictus, while someone with Status (Invictus) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf only has +5, though I suppose they don't get any of the other benefits of Status \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf; still, something to think about.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. I didn't intend it to stack. I'm actually going to modify those by dropping the Social bonus. Since Status can give it anyway. It's kind of silly to double it up, and it's already potentially very powerful.<br /> <br /> New Merit: Envoy to the Others (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Your character is an Envoy to the Others, appointed by the Moon Princess.<br /> Once per chapter, your character can call upon the services of a small cabal of her chosen monster. They\u2019ll assist her in a reasonable time of need.<br /> Additionally, the Envoy can purchase Allies, Contacts, Mentors, Retainers, and Status reflecting supernatural creatures of their given type. While other characters may have access to similar Storyteller characters, the Envoy has knowledge of their abilities, and generally has them at her disposal within reason. For players using other games such as <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, the Status allowed reflects organizational Status Merits within those supernatural groups. While most of these groups are highly secretive and restrictive of membership, agreements in Honshu are such that Yosei diplomats are regularly afforded respect. Status in these organizations is generally limited to three dots.<br /> New Merit: Envoy Assistant (\u2022)<br /> Your character assists an Envoy in official capacity. She can purchase Allies, Contacts, Mentors, Retainers, and Status reflecting supernatural creatures of their given type. As with the Envoy, this comes with a certain knowledge and access beyond what would be considered normal. Status in these organizations is limited to a single dot. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The notion of the YSDF being essentially mercenaries is great, but 300 of them? That's quite a large number, way more than the seemingly lowballed number of Vampires in Tokyo proper, which if I recall was only 200 for the whole city of 13,620,000 people. And that's only a fraction of Honshu's Lost. I mean, I know Honshu total has 103m+ people, but I can never get a head for how many people in a given area are part of a supernatural type. Either way, the notion of people potentially having faerie bodyguards is a pretty good plothook for non-Changeling chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are about 10-20,000 Lost on Honshu. It's about one to every five to ten thousand people. This is very dense. I never say how dense, but I do say it's the most populous per capita. So, most of the world is probably LESS than one in every ten thousand. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965591#post965591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Gotenba, as someone else asked... what about all the <i>gaijin </i>changeling climbing the mountain with the tourists?[/spoiler]<br /> Anyway. Those are my thoughts/questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? I would assume those were exceedingly rare. And if they came, they'd probably have the good sense to figure out what the local freehold structure was like. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, they get beaten up and arrested. Then questioned. Then probably released. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:12:27-07:00","id":965730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965523#post965523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you played <i>Tomb Raider</i> 2013? It's all about a bunch of students and researches getting trapped on a shipwreck island by the powers of a [Sun] queen. Someone in one of the WoD subforums was making their own little Yamatai Dark Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be me. That said, I should probably get back to it sometime. All this stuff on the Yosei might inspire some ideas for that setting.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding LostLight's idea on the Court of Orihime's betrayal, I can definitely see that being set at any point in the Meiji Jidai. Especially since it's the sort of political turmoil that could form in that era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:13:13-07:00","id":965731,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1526\" data-vbnamecard=\"1526\">Diggs</a> Oh, I should have realized the story is an existing story; I mean, that's the whole point of the Freehold story. I'm disappointed the Fire Rat was simply &quot;there's a fire rat, go kill it for me&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> Also probably should have expected there was an answer to the Ulgan thing in Promethean. It's not really a hard number, though both Mortal Remains and Promethean imply that &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">[a]t any given time, there might be one hundred Created walking the Earth.</span></span>&quot; Not hard and fast, but still enough that 12 of a single type in one place is pretty high. Although <i>you</i> also gave hard numbers in Requiem when you said Tokyo has the most vampires, and that Tokyo has 200. That got people extrapolating and making percentages.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A) You're working off incomplete, biased information. It doesn't mean what you think it means. </div> </div> </div> [Need to know more intensifies]<br /> I like the new Fairest version of Calm Before the Storm. &quot;You must spend Willpower to attack&quot; is always a good one, and I can't remember what the 2e version is, but I really liked the 1e version of Splendour of the Envoy's Protection. Except for the one time that I used it and everyone still attacked me.<br /> <br /> Should I also be going through the other Tokyo write ups and looking for references to <i>Evangelion</i> and/or <i>Leverage</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:48:35-07:00","id":965743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965731#post965731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Oh, I should have realized the story is an existing story; I mean, that's the whole point of the Freehold story. I'm disappointed the Fire Rat was simply &amp;quot;there's a fire rat, go kill it for me&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Also probably should have expected there was an answer to the Ulgan thing in Promethean. It's not really a hard number, though both Mortal Remains and Promethean imply that &amp;quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">[a]t any given time, there might be one hundred Created walking the Earth.</span></span>&amp;quot; Not hard and fast, but still enough that 12 of a single type in one place is pretty high. Although <i>you</i> also gave hard numbers in Requiem when you said Tokyo has the most vampires, and that Tokyo has 200. That got people extrapolating and making percentages.<br /> [Need to know more intensifies]<br /> I like the new Fairest version of Calm Before the Storm. &amp;quot;You must spend Willpower to attack&amp;quot; is always a good one, and I can't remember what the 2e version is, but I really liked the 1e version of Splendour of the Envoy's Protection. Except for the one time that I used it and everyone still attacked me.<br /> <br /> Should I also be going through the other Tokyo write ups and looking for references to <i>Evangelion</i> and/or <i>Leverage</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>So. I don't know if I've mentioned this. Tokyo Requiem was supposed to be 1,000. I'm not sure how that got mixed-up. I THINK it was because I said that Tokyo proper might only have 200, but the metro area boasts many more. There was initially a note that the population was supposed to be EXACTLY 1,000, or at least that's what the local Kindred claimed. I.E.: When someone leaves, someone comes in. When someone's Embraced, someone dies. It's a nonsense superstition, but they like it. If I got to do it again, like if I got to do a conglomerate Tokyo book, I'd make it 1,000. <br /> <br /> I can't remember Envoy's Protection in 2e off the top of my hand. But I likewise dig Willpower to attack. It's a little more sensible with 2e rules; it doesn't break Theban Sorcery and shit. <br /> <br /> I don't know if there's a Leverage reference in all the Tokyo sections, but there may be one in every CofD core in general. I want to say the one I remembered in Beast got snipped. But it's been a long time. I wrote a ton of Requiem 2E (like about a third of the book), so there's bound to be some somewhere.<br /> <br /> But Evangelion references? There's one in every Tokyo piece, including Dark Eras Edo. You'll be hard-pressed to find some of them though. I THINK the one in Geist will be pretty obvious, but I can never really tell. But then again, it's also a pretty general thing as opposed to just a line of text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:54:15-07:00","id":965745,"title":"","content":"Inuyasha had a robe of the fire rat. Apparently it is just a rat that has fur that won't burn. At least there is more to it than the shell...and the fifth also failed. I was disappointed in that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:58:13-07:00","id":965749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965745#post965745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inuyasha had a robe of the fire rat. Apparently it is just a rat that has fur that won't burn. At least there is more to it than the shell...and the fifth also failed. I was disappointed in that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Which, if you consider it, is kinda weird. <br /> <br /> But it's a Chinese legendary critter, recognized as part of their zodiac. Which is to say, it doesn't exist. So, when someone's told to get the robe of the fire rat, they just can't. And of course, guys are guys, so they tried forging these impossible items.<br /> <br /> And I imagine Inuyasha is referencing the same legend. I don't know anything about it, but that's almost certainly not a coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:58:25-07:00","id":965750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965743#post965743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geist</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop taunting me! Previews can't come soon enough.<br /> Also, finding references sounds like a challenge.<br /> <br /> I assume Tokyo will play a big part in The Crossover Chronicle?<br /> <br /> And not to get off the topic of Changeling too much [again], but what do you mean about spending Willpower to attack [no longer] breaking Theban Sorcery and shit?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1526\" data-vbnamecard=\"1526\">Diggs</a> Never knew that, though I haven't watched Inuyasha since I was a wee teen, and never kept up with it.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> <i>seemingly</i> impossible! What good are <i>seemingly</i> impossible tasks if true love/determination/guile can't overcome them? If all else fails, hold up the Earth and get someone else to complete your impossible task for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 09-08-2016, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:00:10-07:00","id":965752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965730#post965730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, regarding LostLight's idea on the Court of Orihime's betrayal, I can definitely see that being set at any point in the Meiji Jidai. Especially since it's the sort of political turmoil that could form in that era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Meiji Restoration should be the time frame in which the betrayal should happen- but the question in not only when the Era would be focused during Meiji Jidai, but also in which part of the event itself- personally, I think that the best focus of the Era would be after the said suitor would have finished the &quot;impossible task&quot;, forcing the kingdom into chaos. The True Fae start preparing their Huntsmen and Loyalists to the &quot;imperial wedding ceremony&quot;, which would end with the armies crossing the Hedge and sweep the Freehold. Hysteria spread through the Lost like fire, with the many Courts trying to think just what should they do in order to protect themselves from the incoming disaster, or wonder just how exactly did the impossible quest was completed. The Orihime Court are surprisingly quiet, and many start ask questions. The Moon Princess herself tries to buy time by following every ancient ceremony and tradition which was ever made and using only the rarest and most expensive resources to make a &quot;ceremony worthy for an imperial Princess&quot;. The Envoys seek for leads everywhere in their search after a loophole in the promise- or a proof that the suitor has cheated, and that as such the agreement is null and void. And through all of that time, the Fae walk beside men as the Hedge starts to take root in the world. Everyone know that a danger is coming- but no one is going to attack until the ceremony would finally take place, but the fading borders between the world and Arcadia offer many opportunities for both mortals, changelings and the faerie in the shadows is looming danger. Sure, we all know that in the end, the Moon Princess would stand victorious- but knowing the end doesn't make the story itself any less interesting.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think that somewhere between the end of Edo Jidai and the early Meiji Restoration should be the best time for those events to take place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:02:48-07:00","id":965754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965749#post965749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I imagine Inuyasha is referencing the same legend. I don't know anything about it, but that's almost certainly not a coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, one of the movies was based around Kaguya and the Five Treasures. Sure, they kinda butchered the original story (the Princess was a demon in human skin and the five treasures were used as some form of crazy ritual) but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:08:06-07:00","id":965755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965750#post965750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stop taunting me! Previews can't come soon enough.<br /> Also, finding references sounds like a challenge.<br /> <br /> I assume Tokyo will play a big part in The Crossover Chronicle?<br /> <br /> And not to get off the topic of Changeling too much [again], but what do you mean about spending Willpower to attack [no longer] breaking Theban Sorcery and shit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the old rules, you could only spend one Willpower per turn, period. So anything that forced you to spend Willpower negated your ability to use other powers which required Willpower. <br /> <br /> Like, for example, with old Majesty 5, people had to spend Willpower to attack you. That meant they couldn't use Theban Sorcery to attack you, because they had to spend Willpower in the same turn to activate the spell. (Some people let you stagger out the expenditure, but some rules actively referenced that kind of prohibition.) Now, you just can't spend more than one for a single dice pool. You can spend multiple, to multiple ends. <br /> <br /> And honestly? I know fuck-all about Crossover Chronicle. I learned about it when someone asked me on Twitter from Gen Con if I was developing it. Sounds cool though. I hope I get to be involved, and I hope I get to deliver more Tokyo goodness. <br /> <br /> And by all means, find the references. I'll confirm or deny them. I tend to use references as anchor points for inspiration. I come up with a few ideas that way, it's sort of my version of Oblique Strategies. Then, I build out from there. It's an organic way to keep the words flowing. For Secrets of the Covenants, I used punk songs. For Hurt Locker, I used the works of Clive Barker. For Lost 2E, I used Che Guevara's Guerilla Warfare. Which was actually interesting, because I used it as a foundation for a Shadowrun supplement I worked on years ago, which went a completely different direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:10:49-07:00","id":965756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965754#post965754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, one of the movies was based around Kaguya and the Five Treasures. Sure, they kinda butchered the original story (the Princess was a demon in human skin and the five treasures were used as some form of crazy ritual) but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love fucking with and completely reinterpreting folk tales. I mean, it's what people did with folk tales in the first place, right? We just tend to hear the dominant retelling. <br /> <br /> I find it delightful the way a lot of Japanese media does that. My kids love Yokai Watch, which completely takes this weird, no-holds-barred, tongue-in-cheek approach to folklore that's more invested in adding puns than honoring any sense of authenticity, and it's utterly beautiful for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:14:33-07:00","id":965826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965755#post965755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, in the old rules, you could only spend one Willpower per turn, period. So anything that forced you to spend Willpower negated your ability to use other powers which required Willpower.<br /> <br /> Like, for example, with old Majesty 5, people had to spend Willpower to attack you. That meant they couldn't use Theban Sorcery to attack you, because they had to spend Willpower in the same turn to activate the spell. (Some people let you stagger out the expenditure, but some rules actively referenced that kind of prohibition.) Now, you just can't spend more than one for a single dice pool. You can spend multiple, to multiple ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a subtlety of the new system I had completely glossed over, and I am much profited by the knowledge. Unrelated, I need to read books better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":".  spell better, too 09-08-2016, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:57:20-07:00","id":965853,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> to be fair, in Inuyasha, everyone is a demon.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> I never noticed 2e allows that. Though there are a lot of assumptions from 1e that 2e implicitly does away with, like Firearms defense at close range (unless &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">In close combat, the target\u2019s Defense against Firearms attacks is increased by the gun\u2019s (Size +1)</span></span>&quot; is <i>implicitly</i> stating that you <i>do</i> get Defense in close combat with Firearms; it's not <i>explicitly</i> stated, though, and the Defense section just flat out stats no Defense against Firearms). I also assumed that not being able to use Willpower for <i>other</i> things was intentional for those &quot;spend Willpower to attack&quot; abilities.<br /> <br /> This also makes the Beaten Down Tilt more interesting. I'd assumed with the combat system's high Defenses encouraging spending Willpower on attacks, the Beaten Down Tilt was meant to discourage or make it more difficult to attack (since attacking without Willpower is harder). But if you can spend Defense multiple times in a single turn, it's more like being draining.<br /> <br /> Also, was that intentional, or just a thing that happened? I like 2e overall, but so much of how it came about results in a lot of sloppiness. A lot of stuff really feels like it could have been explained more and made more explicit, because it's so easy to miss things like &quot;it's hard to get a hit in during combat to encourage you to spend Willpower, gang up, and go All-Out&quot;. Or &quot;you can spend Willpower multiple times a turn&quot;. Although I guess it does say &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">You can only spend one point of Willpower per action.</span></span>&quot; so the assumption of one point per turn is really just something people familiar with 1e would assume.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Is there, like, a &quot;changelog&quot; for other things like this? What else am I making the wrong assumptions about?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 09-08-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T16:28:03-07:00","id":965915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965653#post965653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Super good notes. Thank you so much.<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Read the thread before I read the doc, just started and I see what you did there with Yosei/Yousei.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a>, the word fairy is more properly spelled Yousei. That's the joke ( along with tying very well into Lost's themes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T17:59:36-07:00","id":965954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965749#post965749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Which, if you consider it, is kinda weird.<br /> <br /> But it's a Chinese legendary critter, recognized as part of their zodiac. Which is to say, it doesn't exist. So, when someone's told to get the robe of the fire rat, they just can't. And of course, guys are guys, so they tried forging these impossible items.<br /> <br /> And I imagine Inuyasha is referencing the same legend. I don't know anything about it, but that's almost certainly not a coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the wiki, Inuyasha is referencing the Bamboo Cutter and Moonlight Princess story. There really wasn't much to it from the anime. I just remembered the fireproof pelt correlation.<br /> <br /> I particularly like the Bamboo Cutter story when the guy bringing the fake branch was telling an elaborate lie and the 6 jewelers he had help him make the gift barged in to expose him because he hadn't paid them yet. Less fun was when he beat them up later but I guess that was supposed to be his right as a samurai.<br /> <br /> I wasn't completely sure I understood Freehold creation from the rules release, but Tokyo clarified and inspired me to create the twin Freeholds of SD-TJ. So here is what you are responsible for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Tijuana has a reputation for being a wild and violent place so the Freehold myth is based on the Aztec creation story of Five Suns. There are four Courts each based on one of the classical elements and an Aztec creation deity, so judgment, mercy, greed or hardwork, and wrath. The bulwark is an offering to one of the Aztec deities every 20 days with the addition that every 52 years the offerings have to be the real deal complete with human sacrifices. Every year for 5 days the Freehold has a flower war with the local Gentry in the Hedge. Each day a Court pits its warriors against an equal number of Gentry forces with each side trying to capture opposing warriors. At the end of a day the Court leader can choose to symbolically defeated/destroyed like the Court's associated Sun/World to be able to take the place of all the changelings captured that day so they are free for the fifth day. The Fifth Sun leads a number of changelings equal to the total number of Gentry forces captured the four preceding days against the Gentry numbering the total number of changelings captured over the same period. The Changelings have to win on the Fifth Day to keep the Freehold going.<br /> <br /> For San Diego, I went with the Diegueno story of Chaup. Animals and the cardinal directions are important to the stories so there are four Courts based on a direction and a group of animals. The reptiles are witches that give knowledge that oppose the birds that deal with mourning. The predators are the warriors that focus on competition opposing the service oriented prey that focus on running and hiding. The Courts take turns leading the Freehold. Every time the moon is at apogee the Freehold has to recreate the story of Chaup with 2 females, 2 males, and 2 females each from a different Court not in power taking up roles and the new ruler as Chaup. The Gentry get to try to mess with the the actors but only get to try to kill the new Chaup near the end of the story. Chaup has to live to lead the Freehold for another period.<br /> <br /> There are two mysteries of the area. The first is that changelings that return from Arcadia in TJ are always darklings, elementals, or ogres while SD are always fairest, wizened, or beasts. People that are abducted in one city often return in the other city. The second is that each city has its own Gentry that are unable to send their forces across the border. For changelings that think they are safe as soon as they cross the border are mistaken. The two Gentry groups have a deal to share information and swap changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:00:19-07:00","id":965955,"title":"","content":"I thought the o/ou thing was primarily a difference of romanization.<br /> <br /> I really only know because I made a magical girl themed Changeling focused Hunter Conspiracy called the &quot;Bishojou Senshi Yousei Kishi&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:11:39-07:00","id":965958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965752#post965752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think that somewhere between the end of Edo Jidai and the early Meiji Restoration should be the best time for those events to take place.</div> </div> </div> </div>So either during or sometime after the Bakumatsu?<br /> <br /> Hmm. Regarding the betrayal itself, I imagine it could range from being intentional (the Court willingly aided the Gentry in an attempt to avert a future disaster) to having been an accident (a single courtier - or even a small group of courtiers - was manipulated by a very crafty Fae Lord/Lady).<br /> <br /> I imagine the latter being more likely, as it would explain the Orihime Court's silence. They recognize their handiwork in the Moon Princess' dilemma, and they're afraid of the political backlash they will receive... and then there's the impending invasion from Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:19:53-07:00","id":965960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965954#post965954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't completely sure I understood Freehold creation from the rules release, but Tokyo clarified and inspired me to create the twin Freeholds of SD-TJ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are very nice concepts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not sure which I like more. The Sun Courts of Tijuana, or the regional Directional Court of San Diego. For the latter, though, I assume there isn't a fifth Court like the one featured in the Three Kingdoms Dark Era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:32:58-07:00","id":965968,"title":"","content":"This is great stuff. I'm still trying to get a handle on how approaches work in practice though. It's a really cool concept I'm just not sure I understand how to apply it correctly. That said, I dig the super sentai reference, especially since I've been running a Summer Court that requires attacking Fae to send a series of escalating monsters before they can personally take the field. <br /> They even have a Beast &quot;sixth ranger&quot;. As genres go that one's pretty well tilted in the protagonist's favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:01:22-07:00","id":965982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965955#post965955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the o/ou thing was primarily a difference of romanization.<br /> <br /> I really only know because I made a magical girl themed Changeling focused Hunter Conspiracy called the &quot;Bishojou Senshi Yousei Kishi&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Romanization isn't QUITE as standardized as people like to think. Particularly when wordplay comes into play. Little tiny intonation changes and stuff can lead to a lot of fun puns that wouldn't otherwise exist. <br /> <br /> I pronounce it probably a little closer to Yousei. But when writing for a Western audience, I try to favor the simpler forms where possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:22:08-07:00","id":965987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965853#post965853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, was that intentional, or just a thing that happened? I like 2e overall, but so much of how it came about results in a lot of sloppiness. A lot of stuff really feels like it could have been explained more and made more explicit, because it's so easy to miss things like &quot;it's hard to get a hit in during combat to encourage you to spend Willpower, gang up, and go All-Out&quot;. Or &quot;you can spend Willpower multiple times a turn&quot;. Although I guess it does say &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">You can only spend one point of Willpower per action.</span></span>&quot; so the assumption of one point per turn is really just something people familiar with 1e would assume.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Is there, like, a &quot;changelog&quot; for other things like this? What else am I making the wrong assumptions about?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It was intentional. Rose made that call in the CofD core and Requiem 2E. IIRC, GMC didn't actually note that change (it might have, but it's been a while, and frankly I try to avoid reading/referencing GMC because it can lead to subtle conflicts). We had a brief discussion about it. We agreed that it led to too many unintended implications, like Majesty shutting down Theban Sorcery. <br /> <br /> And no, I don't think there's a change log or anything like that. I kinda wish there was. I also kind of wish we had more room to explain and example things. But, I know we were tight with space, and had to make the best with what we had. I'd love to do a &quot;Chronicles of Darkness Pro Edition&quot; or something with a lot more depth and thoroughness, along with pulling back the curtains and showing some of the nuts and bolts with ideas for how to hack it all up and own it. Maybe some day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T20:06:23-07:00","id":966010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965743#post965743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember Envoy's Protection in 2e off the top of my hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Witnesses gain the Swooning Condition toward you and mundane humans can't deliberately attack you as long as you're being nonthreatening.<br /> <br /> (It's a recent acquisition and the direct cause of at least one ongoing fiasco in my playtest game; I've got the rules near to hand.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:16:59-07:00","id":966056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=966010#post966010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Witnesses gain the Swooning Condition toward you and mundane humans can't deliberately attack you as long as you're being nonthreatening.<br /> <br /> (It's a recent acquisition and the direct cause of at least one ongoing fiasco in my playtest game; I've got the rules near to hand.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fucking talking cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:43:13-07:00","id":966069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965960#post965960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are very nice concepts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not sure which I like more. The Sun Courts of Tijuana, or the regional Directional Court of San Diego. For the latter, though, I assume there isn't a fifth Court like the one featured in the Three Kingdoms Dark Era?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I like duality and contrast. I'm having the two freeholds as sort of together while separated by locale. Changelings that want to fight the Fae go join the 5 Suns while those that don't or can't go with the other freehold. The Keepers on the south side are warriors and the ones on the north are witches so it is combat to the south and magic/trickery/traps to the north.<br /> <br /> They just have north, south, east, and west which is convenient because San Diego is divided into North, South, East, and Downtown. They associate colors with direction so I might go with colors for naming the courts. There was a great serpent that came from the west that imparted all knowledge to the people. The spirits of the dead travel east to the ancestral home to dance and the eagle is used for a funeral rite. In the story of Chaup, there are people to the south that eat snakes, rats, and hares so I thought of all the animals that are hunted for food. Chaup is ball lightning that ends up kicking everybody's ass and possibly viewed by surrounding peoples as a demon. It just so happens he travels to live in the north at the end of the story so I left that for the cougars, bears, and coyotes.<br /> <br /> The story of Chaup is about 2 sisters with the youngest having twin boys that grow up and marry 2 sisters with the youngest having a son. All the males are Chaup but only the son survives. Lots of people end up dead but it is from magic and trickery rather than combat. They hunt, craft, cook, sing, play music, and travel in the story. The reason for allowing the Fae to try and kill Chaup is because that is how his grandfather spends his time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:10:27-07:00","id":966337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965955#post965955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the o/ou thing was primarily a difference of romanization.<br /> <br /> I really only know because I made a magical girl themed Changeling focused Hunter Conspiracy called the &quot;Bishojou Senshi Yousei Kishi&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Along with what David said, Japanese isn't even as homogeneous as people think. There are some pretty big regional differences in the language. I've learned some large diffferences in speaking between people from Tokyo and Kyoto for example.<br /> <br /> With Yousei/Yosei, the dictionaries I use have it spelled one way for 'fairie' (\u3088\u3046\u305b\u3044) and the other for 'the years remaining in ones life' (\u3088\u305b\u3044).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:14:45-07:00","id":966493,"title":"","content":"Yep. My city is a hop, skip, and a jump from Tokyo. But we also have a very recognized dialect. In fact, our old people are often completely incoherent to people even a couple of hours' drive away. Our dialect even has a japanese wikipedia page. <br /> <br /> The two terms are separate, with separate kanji. But when said at a good pace, they're almost indistinguishable. I heard the two confused for one another in a drama recently, it's where I got the idea. <br /> <br /> And on television, you often see people from Tokyo/Kanto teasing people from Kansai region over their way of speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:15:01-07:00","id":984510,"title":"","content":"Rereading about these Courts makes me wonder what kind of Court Contracts the Toronto Courts will get. Really, Really curious.<br /> <br /> I mean I know they'll get they court emotion verison of the Emotion Contract, which is like the Fleeting seasonal court contracts from 1e, and a Talespinning Contract which if I had to guess is a contract that draws upon a Courts unique symbols/story, but I have no idea what special unique court contracts each Toronto Court gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:58:16-07:00","id":984656,"title":"","content":"I am really interested in seeing them too! Hopefully good stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Since we're getting finals before editing lately, maybe we'll get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T08:04:51-07:00","id":1550627,"title":"","content":"Is there anyway I can read it? The Google Drive requires permission to read","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T23:22:40-07:00","id":1551111,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoRXgtUjI0alAyc0E/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-PSthKYaX6-96m5tXpW66IQ\" target=\"_blank\">Try this.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"